--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- chain in a short-crested Torsethaugen sea (cos-2s spreading), 300 s
-- Same held-fairlead studless chain as dynamic_chain_waves.dat (50 m depth), here in an irregular
-- sea. The torsethaugen row builds the two-peak Torsethaugen spectrum for Hs = 5.0 m, Tp = 11.0 s
-- (a wind-sea peak and a swell peak split from Hs and Tp). WaveSpreading = 4 spreads each
-- frequency over +/-90 deg about the mean direction with D(theta) ~ cos^8(theta - 30 deg),
-- sampled in WaveDirections bins of WaveComponents components each. The same WaveSeed always
-- gives the same sea; rampTime ramps the wave amplitudes in over the first 20 s. The waves add
-- Morison drag, Froude-Krylov, and buoyancy wetting loads along the line.
